= Naming conventions =

Titles should describe the subject or real MediaWiki object without encoding implementation history.

== Rules ==
* Use configured namespaces rather than simulated namespace-like prefixes.
* Prefer the canonical subject name in Main.
* Use sentence-style descriptive titles for BITwiki meta pages.
* Do not append Revised, Final, New, Styled, Phase 2, or similar workflow state to ordinary canonical titles.
* Use redirects for common alternate names and previous titles.
* Use explicit archive/history titles only when the historical object itself is meaningful.
* Subpages are acceptable when the parent-child relationship is real; do not use them merely to imitate directories.
* Category names should be stable nouns or noun phrases describing an actual class or domain.
* Property names should be clear predicates or attributes and should correspond to implemented semantics.

== Singular and plural ==
Use singular names for individual entity-type concepts and properties where natural. Use plural or collective category titles where they clearly name a class. Consistency matters more than mechanically enforcing one grammatical form.

